{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011W2ncJuk4JPjwRN8qwyQUW","type":"tool_result","content":"94:## INF-001 — Google Sheets Workbook Bootstrap\n95-\n96-- Status baseline: pending\n97-- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n98-- Dependencies: [GOV-001]\n99-- Objective: Create the Panel-Ops workbook with all 16 tabs, exact headers, and seed rows.\n100-- Context: `data-model.md` is normative. Tabs: Customers, Tickets, Parts, Quotations, Quotation_Lines, Payments, Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices, Users, Workflow_States, Activity, Documents, Configuration, Loss_Reasons, Imports.\n101-- Scope: Apps Script setup script (idempotent) that creates tabs + headers; seed Workflow_States (17 states per `workflow-state-machine.md`), Configuration keys (`vat_rate=0.19`, `edge_waste_factor=1.10`, `quotation_validity_hours=48`, `aging_alert_minutes=60`, `transition_matrix` JSON generated from `workflow-state-machine.md`, `sequences`, empty `withholding_rules`, empty `company_legal_info`), Loss_Reasons starter list, 3 Users placeholders (roles management/sales/billing).\n102-- Out of scope: business logic, UI.\n103-- Architectural invariants: header names exactly per `data-model.md`; no extra columns; script idempotent (safe re-run).\n104-- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/setup/**`\n105-- Deliverables: setup script + run evidence (tab list + header screenshots or logged dump).\n106-- Verification commands: script self-check function that reads back all tabs/headers and diffs against embedded schema, logging PASS/FAIL per tab.\n107-- Acceptance criteria: self-check PASS on all 16 tabs; seeds present; re-run makes no changes.\n108-- Rollback notes: workbook is new; delete workbook to roll back.\n109-- Architect notes: keep schema constants in one module for reuse by later tickets.\n110-\n111-## INF-002 — Apps Script Web App Skeleton (API + Auth + Data Layer)\n112-\n113-- Status baseline: pending\n114-- Recommended model: claude-opus-4-8\n115-- Dependencies: [INF-001]\n116-- Objective: Deployable Web App: session identity from Google account, role resolution from Users tab, JSON API router, generic table read layer, single locked write path, ID sequence generator, Activity writer.\n117-- Context: every later module builds on this. ADR-002 write-path rule.\n118-- Scope: `doGet` serves SPA shell; `doPost` JSON API with action routing; `getSession()` (email→role, reject unknown); `db.read(table, filter)`, `db.insert/update(table, row)` wrapped in LockService with atomic sequence increments; `activity.log(...)`; error envelope `{ok:false, error, allowed?}`; deployment config (execute as user accessing, domain-restricted).\n119-- Out of scope: any business module, UI beyond an authenticated \"hello + role\" shell.\n120-- Architectural invariants: role checks server-side; unknown user → 403 page; no physical deletes; writes only via locked path.\n121-- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/core/**`, `src/gas/api/**`, `src/ui/shell/**`\n122-- Deliverables: deployed test Web App URL + module code.\n123-- Verification commands: test function suite (Apps Script) covering: unknown email rejected; sequence increments atomically under loop; insert+read round-trip per table; Activity row appended on write.\n124-- Acceptance criteria: all tests logged PASS; shell loads showing user email + role.\n125-- Rollback notes: undeploy web app.\n126-- Architect notes: this is the foundation — review carefully before accepting.\n127-\n128-## INF-003 — Drive Case-File Automation\n129-\n130-- Status baseline: pending\n131-- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n132-- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n133-- Objective: Create/maintain the `/WOOD_PANEL_OPERATIONS` root and per-order folder trees; upload with naming convention; write-once original-request folder.\n134-- Context: `architecture.md §5`, master doc §12.\n135-- Scope: `drive.ensureRoot()`, `drive.createOrderFolders(ticketId, customerName)` (subfolders 00–07), `drive.storeFile(ticketId, category, blob)` applying naming `ORD-…_*`, Documents row per file, `immutable=true` for category original_request; customer folders under `01_CUSTOMERS`.\n136-- Out of scope: UI upload widgets (APP-002).\n137-- Architectural invariants: nothing in `00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST` is ever overwritten/deleted; every stored file gets a Documents row.\n138-- Files allowed to change: `src/gas/drive/**`\n139-- Deliverables: module + test evidence.\n140-- Verification commands: test creating order tree, storing file in each category, attempting overwrite in original_request (expect rejection), verifying Documents rows.\n141-- Acceptance criteria: tree matches spec exactly; overwrite rejected; rows correct.\n142-- Rollback notes: test folders under a `_TEST` prefix, deletable.\n143-- Architect notes: use Drive folder IDs in Documents, not paths.\n144-\n145-## APP-001 — Customers Module\n146-\n147-- Status baseline: pending\n148-- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n149-- Dependencies: [INF-002]\n150-- Objective: Customer CRUD (soft delete) + search, per `data-model.md#Customers`, roles M/S.\n151-- Context: `permissions-matrix.md`.\n152-- Scope: API actions create/update/list/search/deactivate; duplicate warning on (`id_type`,`id_number`); UI form + list (Spanish).\n153-- Out of scope: purchase history, credit fields.\n154-- Architectural invariants: billing role read-only here; required fields enforced server-side.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfaf515c-a027-44c3-87b0-f5ccc9482619","uuid":"60e8a527-03ef-4ae7-a1d6-22e97703ed15","timestamp":"2026-07-18T03:35:31.478Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"94:## INF-001 — Google Sheets Workbook Bootstrap\n95-\n96-- Status baseline: pending\n97-- Recommended model: claude-sonnet-5\n98-- Dependencies: [GOV-001]\n99-- Objective: Create the Panel-Ops workbook with all 16 tabs, exact headers, and seed rows.\n100-- Context: `data-model.md` is normative. Tabs: Customers, Tickets, Parts, Quotations, Quotation_Lines, Pa